\fs28 \cf0 This will install all of the screen savers system-wide. 
It will take around 450 MB.\
\

\f1\b Installation will take several minutes, and the progress bar will not 
move for most of that time. Just wait it out! 
\f0\b0 \
\
After installation, select the screen saver at the bottom of the list that is 
called 
\f2\i\b "Random XScreenSaver"
\f3\b0  
\f0\i0 instead of the built-in one called just 
\f2\i\b "Random"
\f3\b0  
\f0\i0 -- you can choose how long a saver should run before a new one is 
selected, and you can un-check the ones that you don't like.\
\
Apple really tries to hide the screen savers these days!\
\
To see them all, select 
\f2\i\b "System Settings", 
\f0\i0\b0 select 
\f2\i\b "Wallpaper", 
\f0\i0\b0 then the 
\f2\i\b "Screen Saver..." 
\f0\i0\b0 button at the top, then scroll 
\f3\i all the way down 
\f0\i0 to the last row that says 
\f2\i\b "Other", 
\f0\i0\b0 and finally, click 
\f2\i\b "Show All (324)". 
\f3\b0 Easy! 
\f0\i0 \
\
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
